{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Y el cananeo estaba entonces en la tierra.</b> Rashi explicó que aquel iba conquistando a la descendencia de Shem, pues la tierra había caído en la porción de Shem cuando Noaj dividió la tierra entre sus hijos. Y es desconcertante, pues en la parashat shelaj lejá Rashi explicó sobre el versículo ״וחברון שבע שנים נבנתה״ que Mitzrayim gave it to his firstborn son, but it was built from everything good, like one of the seven of Tzoan, and so it is concluded in Sotah, chapter ואלו נאמרין — thus it implies that Hebron, which is in the land of Israel, fell to the portion of Ham. One may answer that it is a dispute, for in Torat Kohanim it concludes: for what reason did the Canaanites merit to dwell in their land 47 years more than the Egyptians? How? Seven years that Hebron was built before Tzoan of Egypt, and forty years that Israel dwelt in the wilderness after Egypt was destroyed — because they set aside a portion for Abraham the righteous and said to him: ״נשיא אלהים אתה בתוכנו״."], :book "genesis", :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :es, :chapter 12, :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:25:08.063404905Z", :translated-from :en, :model "glm-5.2"}